From 9e9088c0312ae09f991c9a5067905ae8700378fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: pull the bottom tab sheet up from the button bar

An upward drag on the five-button bottom bar now opens the bottom-bar
tab sheet 1:1, like the address-bar pull. Once the move is upward, past
touch slop and steeper than it is sideways, the bar intercepts the
gesture, cancels the pressed button so a tap target such as + does not
fire, and drives the sheet through the same pull calls the address bar
uses. The release velocity from a VelocityTracker feeds the spring
settle.

Taps still press the buttons with no added delay, and horizontal drags
keep their meaning. The pull only runs when the tabs style is Sheet and
the address bar is at the bottom, so the side drawer and the top-bar
sheet are unchanged.
